  "result": "I found the bug and wrote up the fix, but haven't changed any code yet because plan mode is on. I couldn't find the tool for submitting the plan for approval, so I'm asking here: tell me to go ahead and I'll apply it.\n\n**Cause:** the problem only happens when the range excludes its endpoint (`min_open` or `max_open`) and clamping is on. The code that picks the clamped value (`IntRange._clamp`, `src/click/types.py:754`) does `return bound - dir`. That moves the value one step outside the range instead of one step inside it:\n- `IntRange(0, 5, min_open=True, clamp=True)` turns `-3` into `-1` instead of `1`.\n- `IntRange(0, 5, max_open=True, clamp=True)` turns `10` into `6` instead of `4`.\n\nRanges that include their endpoints clamp to the endpoint directly, which is why the existing tests pass.\n\n**Fix:** change that line to `return bound + dir`.\n\n**Tests:** add four cases to `test_range` in `tests/test_types.py` covering the excluded-endpoint cases above, then run `pytest tests/test_types.py` and the full test suite.\n\nThe plan is saved at `<home>\\.claude\\plans\\some-users-report-that-wise-otter.md`.",
